From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Royere <troyere@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:37:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nvport: fix month and year boundaries in wall-time conversion

The remaining day count is zero-based, so a full month or year must be consumed when the count equals its length. Using strict comparisons leaves the first day of a new period in the preceding month or year, producing dates such as September 31.

Use inclusive comparisons in both loops so the residual day count stays within the selected month and year.

Upstream PR: https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules/pull/1432
---
 src/nvidia/src/libraries/nvport/time/time_generic.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/libraries/nvport/time/time_generic.c b/src/nvidia/src/libraries/nvport/time/time_generic.c
index 784a28d2..da346ff9 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/libraries/nvport/time/time_generic.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/libraries/nvport/time/time_generic.c
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ _portTimeUnixTimeToDate
     *pYear = 1970;
     *pDay = 0;
 
-    while (t > _portTimeDaysInYear(*pYear))
+    while (t >= _portTimeDaysInYear(*pYear))
     {
         t -= _portTimeDaysInYear(*pYear);
         (*pYear)++;
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ _portTimeUnixTimeToDate
     if (_portTimeIsLeapYear(*pYear))
         daysInMonth[1]++;
 
-    for (*pMonth = 0; t > daysInMonth[*pMonth]; (*pMonth)++)
+    for (*pMonth = 0; t >= daysInMonth[*pMonth]; (*pMonth)++)
         t -= daysInMonth[*pMonth];
 
     (*pMonth)++;
